    "Model exhibits severe underestimation bias when recent history shows a sharp upward spike (e.g., >89 EUR) followed by volatility; forecasts fail to capture the momentum of the preceding days.",
    "Forecasts display significant lag in reacting to sentiment spikes (0.33); actual outcomes often surge 5-10% higher than predicted within 2-4 days after a high-sentiment event.",
    "Model assumes linear growth but true outcomes exhibit mean-reverting volatility; forecasts overshoot the initial spike level while underestimating the subsequent consolidation phase.",
    "When sentiment history contains multiple low values (0.00) interspersed with single spikes, the model ignores the 'setup' phase and fails to predict the magnitude of the breakout.",
    "Horizon-specific error: Model predicts a smooth upward trend, whereas true outcomes show high-frequency oscillation around a rising mean, causing forecast lines to diverge sharply from actual paths."
  ]
